  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Minburn Technology Group has $767M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Minburn Technology Group won 453 awards so far this fiscal year. Minburn Technology Group has an average award size of $1.7M. Minburn Technology Group obligations are down 18.9% year over year. The current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date obligations. The largest single annual obligations on record in the listed years are FY25 with $946M and FY24 with $927M, while FY21 through FY23 show earlier levels of activity: $559M, $494M, and $796M respectively. The company’s obligations are concentrated in a few agencies and in information and software-related NAICS categories, which drive most of the fiscal-year-to-date totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies account for the most obligations?",
        "body": "General Services Administration obligated $261M, making GSA the largest buyer from Minburn Technology Group in FY2026 to date. Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $143M and Department of State obligated $140M. Department of the Treasury and Department of Energy follow with $78.1M and $55.6M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are obligations concentrated by NAICS market?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services accounts for $396M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Software Publishers accounts for $352M of obligations. Other listed markets include Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $11.1M and Computer Terminal and Other Computer Peripheral Equipment Manufacturing at $8.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
